			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2829541">
									

<p>Thinking about this from your perspective, as someone who read the 'second' page first, it occurs to me that there's not much in the way of information on the first page that isn't on the second. If this were just ESCP-3072, it might be a worthwhile format screw a la Cross Cross City or something, and a read could figure out what the original article looked like by picking out the colored text. The main thing that would be lost by reducing this just to the ESCP format would be the redactions in the ticker tape readout, of course, but there's probably a way or two to make that happen (since it was actually kind of fun).</p>
<p>Point being, I initially came down hard on this, but I don't want to quash experimentation. I think it'd be worth changing things around to make this work better, if, indeed, it ends up not working.</p>

